---
title: "[viz.plot_influence()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}"
body-classes: doc-api-page
page-navigation: false
html-table-processing: none
---

::: {.doc-subject}

Diagnostic scatter plots for identifying influential observations in a Cox model.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/viz/_influence.py#L52-L127){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
viz.plot_influence(
    cox,
    *,
    highlight=3,
    panels=None,
    title=None,
    backend="altair",
    width=240,
    height=200
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Produces a horizontal row of panels plotting key diagnostics against the linear predictor. The
most influential observations (by likelihood displacement) are highlighted in red and labeled
with their observation number.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[cox]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A fitted `CoxPH` model.

<code>[highlight]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[3]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Number of most influential observations to highlight and label (default `3`). Set to `0` to
    disable highlighting.

<code>[panels]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[str, ...] | list[str] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Which diagnostic panels to show. Each name is a column from `influence_diagnostics()`. The
    default is `("deviance", "leverage", "ld")`.

<code>[title]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Optional supertitle for the combined chart.

<code>[backend]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Literal[[&quot;altair&quot;]{.st}, [&quot;plotnine&quot;]{.st}]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;altair&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Plotting backend: `"altair"` (default) or `"plotnine"`.

<code>[width]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[240]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Width of each panel in pixels (Altair) or inches (plotnine).

<code>[height]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[200]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Height of each panel in pixels (Altair) or inches (plotnine).
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [alt.Chart or plotnine.ggplot]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A composite chart (Altair `HConcatChart`) or a faceted plotnine plot.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#795b8704 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

lung = gw.load_dataset("lung", backend="polars")
y = gw.Surv.right(lung["time"], event=(lung["status"] == 2))
cox = gw.CoxPH().fit(y, lung[["age", "sex"]])

gw.plot_influence(cox)
```

